\DOC MAYCHANGE_IDEMPOT_TAC

\TYPE {MAYCHANGE_IDEMPOT_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves goals stating that a state-relation built from {,,}-composed
{MAYCHANGE}/{ASSIGNS} components (or a trivial relation) composed with itself
equals itself, closing the goal.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. It applies to a goal whose conclusion is an
equation {t ,, u = u}, where {u} is a (possibly nested and parenthesised)
{,,}-composition of relation components and {t} is that same composition
bracketed as a single unit. The assumptions are left untouched and play no
role: the same closure is observed with any assumption list, including long
lists of arithmetic, memory-disjointness, register-read and {ensures}
hypotheses.
{
      A ?- t ,, u = u
      ===============  MAYCHANGE_IDEMPOT_TAC
      (no goals)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the tactic closes the goal, always on conclusions of
this self-composition-equals-itself shape; no other kind of outcome appears.

\ENDDOC
